## Names of the built-in devices (`komponist-builtin`, `Internal::name_in`). Brand names stay; generic ones translate.

# Name of the FM synthesizer (brand).
device-name-hexa = Hexa
device-description-hexa = Six-operator FM synthesizer.

# Name of the virtual-analog synthesizer (brand).
device-name-volt = Volt
device-description-volt = Virtual analog synthesizer with two oscillators.

# Name of the wavetable synthesizer (brand).
device-name-surf = Surf
device-description-surf = Wavetable synthesizer with two oscillators.

# Name of the drum sampler.
device-name-sampler = Klopfer
device-description-sampler = Eight-pad drum sampler.

# Name of the general-purpose sampler.
device-name-general-sampler = Sampler
device-description-general-sampler = Sampler for chromatic playback and slices.

# Name of the compressor (brand).
device-name-presse = Presse
device-description-presse = Compressor with a sidechain input.

# Name of the equalizer.
device-name-eq = EQ
device-description-eq = Parametric equalizer for shaping sound.

# Name of the delay.
device-name-delay = Delay
device-description-delay = Echo effect with rhythmic repeats.

# Name of the reverb.
device-name-hall = Reverb
device-description-hall = Adds reverberation to instruments and audio.

# Name of the limiter.
device-name-limiter = Limiter
device-description-limiter = Limits peak levels.

# Name of the arpeggiator MIDI effect.
device-name-arpeggiator = Arpeggiator
device-description-arpeggiator = Plays held notes in a rhythmic sequence.

# Name of the scale MIDI effect.
device-name-tonleiter = Scale
device-description-tonleiter = Maps incoming notes to a scale.
